  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs of bwami, the graded initiation association of the Lega of South Kivu and Maniema, sung during the rites through which members rise in grade, where sung aphorisms accompany the display of carved ivory and wooden figures. Daniel Biebuyck documented and recorded the rites during his fieldwork among the Lega in the early 1950s. Generic drum and shaker cards stand in for the rites' percussion.",
